        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "13298796_3",
          "text": "<p>\r\n\tA shift reduce parser carries out the actions specified within braces after the RHS of every production rule:</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<img style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" alt=\"\" src=\"assets/images_me25/img_2863.png\" /></p>\r\n<p>\r\n\tWhat is the translation for ‘<em>aaaabcc</em>’ ?</p><br><table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:10px;\">\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(A)</td><td>11231</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(B)</td><td>11233</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(C)</td><td>23131</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(D)</td><td>23321</td></tr>\n            </table>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.33",
          "tags": "Made Easy",
          "category": "Technical",
          "solution": "<p>\r\n\t(c)</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<img style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" alt=\"\" src=\"assets/images_me25/img_2864.png\" /></p>",
          "video": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1034199105"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "13298796_4",
          "text": "<p>\r\n\tWhich of the following parameter is not included in the activation record of recursive function call?</p><br><table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:10px;\">\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(A)</td><td>Local variables of function</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(B)</td><td>Return value of function</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(C)</td><td>Global variables of program</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(D)</td><td>Access link</td></tr>\n            </table>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.33",
          "tags": "Made Easy",
          "category": "Technical",
          "solution": "<p>\r\n\t(c)<br />\r\n\tGlobal variables section is included in the &ldquo;main&rdquo; activation record of the program. All activation record makes access link to the &ldquo;main&rdquo; to access the global variables.</p>",
          "video": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1034199140"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "13298796_5",
          "text": "<p>\r\n\tA grammar that has not any epsilon productions and also free from unit productions. The maximum number of reduce moves that can be taken during bottom up evaluation of 25 token string by bottom up parsers is ________.</p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "49",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.00",
          "tags": "Made Easy",
          "category": "Technical",
          "solution": "<p>\r\n\t49<br />\r\n\tMaximum number of reduce moves for <em>n</em> token = 2<em>n</em> &ndash; 1<br />\r\n\tSo, for 25 tokens = 2 &times; 25 &ndash; 1 = 49</p>",
          "video": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1034199179"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "13298796_6",
          "text": "<p>\r\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\r\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Handle is a sub-string that matches right side of production whose reduction to non-terminal on left sides of production represents one step along the reverse of left-most derivation.<br />\r\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Viable prefixes of grammar G are those prefixes of right sentential form that appears on stack of shift reduce parsing.<br />\r\n\tWhich of the following is true?</p><br><table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:10px;\">\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(A)</td><td><p>\r\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p></td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(B)</td><td><p>\r\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(C)</td><td><p>\r\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(D)</td><td><p>\r\n\tNeither <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> nor <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></td></tr>\n            </table>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.33",
          "tags": "Made Easy",
          "category": "Technical",
          "solution": "<p>\r\n\t(b)<br />\r\n\t&bull; Handle is a sub-string that matches right side of production whose reduction to non-terminal on left hand side of production represents one step along the reverse of right-most derivation.<br />\r\n\t&bull; Viable prefixes are those prefixes of right sentential form that can appear on the stack of a shift reduce parser.</p>",
          "video": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1034199245"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "13298796_7",
          "text": "<p>\r\n\tConsider the following CFG:</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<img style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" alt=\"\" src=\"assets/images_me25/img_2865.png\" /></p>\r\n<p>\r\n\tThe above grammar is</p><br><table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:10px;\">\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(A)</td><td>Ambiguous and left recursive</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(B)</td><td>Unambiguous and non left recursive</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(C)</td><td>Ambiguous and non left recursive</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(D)</td><td>Unambiguous and left recursive</td></tr>\n            </table>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.33",
          "tags": "Made Easy",
          "category": "Technical",
          "solution": "<p>\r\n\t(c)</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<img style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" alt=\"\" src=\"assets/images_me25/img_2866.png\" /></p>",
          "video": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1034199266"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "13298796_8",
          "text": "<p>\r\n\tConsider the following grammar:</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<img style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" alt=\"\" src=\"assets/images_me25/img_2867.png\" /></p>\r\n<p>\r\n\tWhere S and X are non-terminals and a, b are terminals. Which of the following can be the viable prefixes?</p><br><table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:10px;\">\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(A)</td><td>baab</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(B)</td><td>aab</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(C)</td><td>aaabab</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(D)</td><td>bbbaX</td></tr>\n            </table>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.33",
          "tags": "Made Easy",
          "category": "Technical",
          "solution": "<p>\r\n\t(b)<br />\r\n\tViable prefixes: Combination of non-terminal and terminal which can be in the stack during parsing is called viable prefix.<br />\r\n\tA handle X&rarr; b is available. So whenever terminal b is encounter it is popped out before inserting new element into the stack.<br />\r\n\tOption (a) is wrong because before popping &lsquo;b&rsquo; element &lsquo;aab&rsquo; is inserted.<br />\r\n\tOption (b) is correct after &lsquo;b&rsquo; no element has inserted.<br />\r\n\tSo, option (c) and (d) also incorrect.</p>",
          "video": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1034199313"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "13298796_9",
          "text": "<p>\r\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\r\n\t(i) Type checking is done during all the phases especially in syntax analysis phase.<br />\r\n\t(ii) Target code generation phase is machine independent code generation.<br />\r\n\t(iii) SDT with only synthesized attribute, always have a order of evaluation.<br />\r\n\t(iv) Symbol table is constructed during analysis part of compiler<br />\r\n\tWhich of the above is correct?</p><br><table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:10px;\">\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(A)</td><td>(i) and (ii) only</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(B)</td><td>(iii) and (iv) only</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(C)</td><td>(ii) and (iv)</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(D)</td><td>(i) and (ii) only</td></tr>\n            </table>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.66",
          "tags": "Made Easy",
          "category": "Technical",
          "solution": "<p>\r\n\t(b)<br />\r\n\t&bull; Type checking is done during semantic analysis phase.<br />\r\n\t&bull; Target code generation is machine specific.<br />\r\n\t&bull; SDT with only synthesized attribute does not have any cyclic dependency. So always have order of evaluation.<br />\r\n\t&bull; Symbol table is constructed during the lexical, syntax and semantic analysis phase.</p>",
          "video": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1034199350"
        },
