        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "13298796_12",
          "text": "<p>\r\n\tWhich of the following is not a token in C language?</p><br><table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:10px;\">\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(A)</td><td>Semicolon</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(B)</td><td>Identifier</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(C)</td><td>Keyword</td></tr>\n                <tr><td style=\"width:30px; vertical-align:top;\">(D)</td><td>White space</td></tr>\n            </table>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.33",
          "tags": "Made Easy",
          "category": "Technical",
          "solution": "<p>\r\n\t(d)<br />\r\n\tC tokens are:<br />\r\n\t1. Keywords<br />\r\n\t2. Identifiers<br />\r\n\t3. Constants<br />\r\n\t4. Symbols ( ;, (, ), }, {, etc.)<br />\r\n\t5. Operators<br />\r\n\tWhite spaces are used to separate the tokens but they are not counted as a token. White spaces are ignored while identifying the tokens.</p>",
          "video": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1034199448"
        },
